        <section type="header">
            <text>Chapter 21: The Progressive Era</text>
        </section>
        
        <section type="body">
            <paragraph id="1">
                <text>The Progressive Era (1890-1920) was a period of widespread social activism and political reform across the United States. The movement primarily targeted political machines and their bosses, working to eliminate corruption in government.</text>
            </paragraph>
            
            <paragraph id="2">
                <text>Progressives sought to address the problems caused by industrialization, urbanization, immigration, and political corruption. They believed that government should be the primary agent of change.</text>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        
